# Blitz Supabase schema (source of truth)

**Update this file whenever you add or change** `supabase/migrations/*.sql`.

Last aligned with: `001_initial.sql`, `002_roles_and_admin.sql`, `003_admin_email_login.sql`

## ER diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
  auth_users ||--o| user_roles : has
  auth_users ||--o| admin_profiles : has
  auth_users ||--o| user_sync_meta : has
  auth_users ||--o{ sync_documents : owns
  auth_users ||--o{ synced_applications : owns
  auth_users ||--o| license_entitlements : has
  auth_users ||--o{ admin_audit_log : actor
  auth_users ||--o{ admin_audit_log : target

  auth_users {
    uuid id PK
    text email
  }

  user_roles {
    uuid user_id PK_FK
    app_role role "user|admin|developer"
    uuid granted_by FK
    timestamptz granted_at
    timestamptz updated_at
  }

  admin_profiles {
    uuid user_id PK_FK
    text email
    boolean allow_email_login "developer admin-portal OTP"
    timestamptz created_at
    timestamptz last_seen_at
  }

  user_sync_meta {
    uuid user_id PK_FK
    int schema_version
    timestamptz last_full_sync_at
    text encryption_version
    timestamptz created_at
    timestamptz updated_at
  }

  sync_documents {
    uuid id PK
    uuid user_id FK
    text doc_key "cv_text|preferences|ai_config|..."
    text ciphertext "E2EE JSON blob"
    text content_hash
    timestamptz updated_at
    text device_id
    timestamptz deleted_at
    timestamptz created_at
  }

  synced_applications {
    uuid id PK_FK
    uuid user_id FK
    text ciphertext "E2EE application record"
    text content_hash
    timestamptz updated_at
    text device_id
    timestamptz deleted_at
    timestamptz created_at
  }

  license_entitlements {
    uuid user_id PK_FK
    text tier "free|pro"
    text source
    timestamptz expires_at
    int applications_used
    text license_key_hash
    timestamptz updated_at
    timestamptz created_at
  }

  admin_audit_log {
    uuid id PK
    uuid actor_id FK
    text action
    uuid target_user_id FK
    jsonb meta
    timestamptz created_at
  }
```

## Extension sync keys (`sync_documents.doc_key`)

Encrypted client-side (see `popup/src/lib/sync-payload.js`):

| doc_key | Notes |
|---------|--------|
| `cv_text` | Base CV |
| `linkedin_profile_text` | LinkedIn export text |
| `user_profile` | Name, contact, work auth, skills |
| `preferences` | Cover letter mode, prompt parts, daily limit, template id |
| `appearance` | Theme / mode |
| `cv_html_template` | PDF HTML template |
| `ai_config` | **provider + model only** (no API key) |
| `license` | **tier + usage** (no license key string) |

**Local-only:** `ai_config.apiKey`, `license.key`, pending job/queue, auth session, sync crypto state.

## RLS helpers

- `public.get_my_role()` → `app_role`
- `public.has_min_role(required)` → admin+ for reads across users
- `public.is_developer()` → role management

## Related apps

| App | Auth | DB access |
|-----|------|-----------|
| Chrome extension | User JWT | `sync_*` own rows; E2EE |
| Admin dashboard (`admin/`) | Staff JWT | RLS `admin` / `developer` |
| Edge Functions | Service role | `license_entitlements`, account delete |
